  "scale_difference_note": "Beijing train PM2.5 mean 99.0 ug/m3 (std 91.7, max 994) vs. Fontibon train PM2.5 mean 18.9 ug/m3 (std 10.8, max 101). The absolute PM2.5 level and spread differ by roughly a factor of 5 between domains (this is why each domain keeps its OWN MinMax scaler — see docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ASSUMPTIONS.md). The transfer hypothesis for Config B/C/D is NOT that absolute PM2.5 levels transfer, but that TEMPORAL structure (autocorrelation, hourly profile shape) captured by the encoder/decoder may partially transfer despite the level/scale difference -- the standardized Wasserstein distance above is the quantitative counterpart of that hypothesis (comparing SHAPE of the distributions, with the level/scale difference removed by standardization).",
